</head>
<body>
<div class="report-container">

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">A Historical Analysis (1970 – 2026)</div>
  <div class="meta">
    <span>Dataset: {n} monthly observations</span>
    <span>Period: Jan 1970 – {rows[-1]['date'][:7]}</span>
    <span>Generated: {datetime.now().strftime('%B %d, %Y')}</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- KPI STRIP -->
<div class="kpi-strip">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">${min_price:.2f} – ${max_price:.2f}</div>
    <div class="label">Overall Price Range</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{cagr * 100:.2f}%</div>
    <div class="label">CAGR ({first_year}–{last_year})</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">${abs(max_mom_abs['abs_change']):.2f}</div>
    <div class="label">Max MoM Change (abs)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{highest_avg_decade['decade']}</div>
    <div class="label">Highest Avg Price Decade</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">${std_dev:.2f}</div>
    <div class="label">Std Deviation</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- CONTENT -->
<div class="content">

<!-- TOC -->
<div class="toc">
  <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#executive-overview">Executive Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#long-term-trend">Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</a></li>
    <li><a href="#decade-by-decade">Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</a></li>
    <li><a href="#volatility-and-shocks">Price Volatility &amp; Major Shocks</a></li>
    <li><a href="#statistical-summary">Statistical Summary &amp; Distribution</a></li>
    <li><a href="#outlook-and-conclusions">Outlook &amp; Conclusions</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW -->
<h2 id="executive-overview">1. Executive Overview</h2>
<p>This report analyzes {n} monthly observations of global crude oil prices from January 1970 through {rows[-1]['date'][:7]}, spanning more than five decades of energy market history. The data reveals a commodity that has undergone profound structural transformations — from the fixed-price regime of the early 1970s, through the seismic shocks of OPEC embargoes and gulf wars, to the financialization and shale-driven volatility of the 21st century.</p>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Key Findings:</strong> Crude oil prices ranged from ${min_price:.2f}/bbl to ${max_price:.2f}/bbl over the full period, a range of ${price_range:.2f}. The compound annual growth rate from 1970 to {last_year} stands at {cagr * 100:.2f}%, though this headline figure masks enormous cyclical variation. The {highest_avg_decade['decade']} recorded the highest average monthly price at ${highest_avg_decade['mean']:.2f}/bbl, while the largest single-month price swing was ${abs(max_mom_abs['abs_change']):.2f}/bbl ({max_mom_abs['to_date'][:7]}).
</div>

<p>The overall trajectory is one of <strong>punctuated equilibrium</strong>: long stretches of relative stability interrupted by violent dislocations tied to geopolitical conflict, supply disruptions, and demand collapses. Prices in the early 1970s hovered below $3/bbl before the first oil shock catapulted them above $10; by 2008, they briefly surpassed $130 before crashing during the financial crisis; and in 2020, the COVID-19 demand shock drove prices to historic lows before a sharp recovery. Understanding these dynamics is essential for any analyst seeking to contextualize current market conditions.</p>

<!-- SECTION 2: LONG-TERM TREND -->
<h2 id="long-term-trend">2. Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
<p>The full time series below presents the complete monthly price history. Several structural regimes are immediately visible: the low and stable pre-1973 era, the step-change during the oil crises, the secular decline of the 1980s–1990s, the super-cycle of the 2000s, and the elevated-volatility environment of the 2010s–2020s.</p>

<div class="chart-wrap">
  <canvas id="chartLongTerm" height="400"></canvas>
</div>

<h3>Major Inflection Points</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Period</th><th>Event</th><th>Price Move</th><th>Structural Impact</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1973–1974</td><td>OPEC Oil Embargo</td><td>${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1973-01-01'][0]:.2f} → ${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1974-01-01'][0]:.2f} (+{(([r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1974-01-01'][0] / [r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1973-01-01'][0]) - 1) * 100:.0f}%)</td><td>Ended era of cheap oil; established OPEC pricing power</td></tr>
    <tr><td>1979–1981</td><td>Iranian Revolution &amp; Iran-Iraq War</td><td>${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1979-01-01'][0]:.2f} → ${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1981-01-01'][0]:.2f}</td><td>Doubled prices; triggered conservation and alternative supply investment</td></tr>
    <tr><td>1986</td><td>Saudi Market Share War</td><td>${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1986-01-01'][0]:.2f} → ${[r['price'] for r in rows if r['date']=='1986-04-01'][0]:.2f}</td><td>Collapsed prices; ended OPEC's ability to defend floor</td></tr>
