<p>The decade opened with prices recovering above $100/bbl, supported by post-crisis demand growth and supply concerns (Libya, Iran sanctions). But the US shale boom fundamentally altered the supply landscape, and OPEC's November 2014 decision not to cut output triggered a price war. Prices fell from ${d2010['max']:.2f}/bbl to below $30 by early 2016. The decade averaged ${d2010['mean']:.2f}/bbl with a CV of {d2010['cv']:.1f}% — high volatility driven by the 2014–2016 collapse and partial recovery.</p>

<h3>2020s: Pandemic, Recovery, and Geopolitical Risk</h3>
